mantle rm289
state ready
dialect plain
accent light broad
tier standard
written_for rm_mathis_slagwell
title the bearer of the spare napkin
fits stage=adult|old
prefers warmth=warm honesty=plain
traits temper=even talk=plain warmth=warm humour=none honesty=plain piety=ordinary drive=steady
quirk smells_faintly_of_smoke_whatever_the_weather
likes oatcakes riddles quiet_chapel autumn_wind
dislikes gulls smoke
fears embarrassing_somebody_in_public
hopes keeping_one_clean_square_to_spare
topics friends +0.6 faith +0.4 food +0.3 pastimes +0.3
styles comfort=quiet gossip=careful refuse=plain tease=gentle
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# rolls an extra clean napkin inside a smoky cuff and offers kindness with eyes deliberately elsewhere.
words
oath! = Soot on my oatcake | Ash in my clean cuff
saying! = Fold the kindness small | Leave one side unstained
nap = a white napkin | a square of linen
oatbit = a split oatcake | a crisp little round
napfold = a narrow roll | a tucked corner
ashmark = a thumb of grey | a whorl of soot
cuffend = a frayed wristband | my dark cuff
carrybit = an easy sling | a thick cord
churchbit = an empty seat | a bare stretch of bench
ruffbit = a brush of stiff fur | a patch of rough coat
autumnbit = a sharp autumn gust | a cold leaf-scented breeze
butter = a soft yellow shaving | a little dab of butter
towelrag = an old wiping cloth | a rough square
riddlemark = a crooked little clue | a puzzle in a few words

grown

opinion strangers for 1 : A clean square can be passed without stopping to ask who needs it.
opinion houses against 1 : A crest doesn't keep soot off a wet face any better than a cheap cuff.
opinion church for 1 : Nobody comes asking for your next pair of hands when a chapel's quiet.
opinion sump for 1 : We know better than to stare at somebody standing very bravely through a rough minute.
opinion dole for 2 : An oatcake given freely tastes better than a whole supper bought with embarrassment.
opinion road mixed 1 : Some journeys are kindest when you have just one end of what needs carrying.
line greet : Stand by my clean side. The other one's a little smoky.
line greet.return : There you are. No straps to hold just now.
line greet [here.time=dawn] : Morning. I've a clean start tucked inside my cuff.
line farewell : Hope the wind meets you on the kinder cheek.
line farewell.return : Take your share of the clean air with you.
line react.news : I'll get the grey off my fingers before I touch that.
line react.news.new : There's a fresh fold in what I thought I'd understood.
line react.news.known : That patch had shown through already.
line react.news.doubt : There's more grey round those words than I'd pass along.
line react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|loss|theft|assault|arrest|crime] : There's a clean square here if somebody wants it.
line react.news.glad [topic.kind=birth|marriage|work|apprentice|succession] : Fine cause for getting out the better butter.
line ask.how : Are you getting your share of the easier end?
line answer.how : A little smoky outside and reasonably clear within.
line decline : I'll carry your parcel. That private business can stay behind.
line thank : You noticed and kept your cleverness quiet.
line sympathise : I'll look the other way while you have a moment.
line reassure : Nobody's taking a reckoning of wet cheeks here.
line accept_decline : Then I shall leave the offer tucked away.
line deflect_thanks : It's only cloth. It'll wash and do another kindness.
line accept_preclose : Walk on while there's a bit of quiet for it.
line ack : I believe I've found the useful corner of that.

scene friends_1
when topic=friends
does offer / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I've got #nap# rolled inside my cuff if a friend needs a minute. | There are two clean corners in this fold, and I'd spare either one.
b : Won't your smoky cuff stain it?
a : I roll the white part inwards. A clean face needn't carry my trade marks.

scene work_1
when topic=work self.trade_words
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : My work goes by #self.trade_words#. I keep cloth between the strap and a bare shoulder. | If there's carrying in the day I want a rag I don't mind spoiling.
b : Why keep a spare one clean?
a : A sore shoulder can bear a stain. An eye full of grit deserves clean linen.

scene food_1
when topic=food self.likes=oatcakes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I can break an oatcake without losing more than two crumbs. | I'll butter the ragged edge first when a cake breaks unevenly.
b : Why start there?
a : So neither of us can see at once which half was the accident.

scene pastimes_1
when topic=pastimes self.likes=riddles
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : What gives its cleanest face to a stranger and keeps its dirtiest to itself? | What comes home folded round the bit it gave away?
b : Something stitched?
a : My napkin, after I lend a corner. Your answer came very close to the seam.

scene faith_1
when topic=faith self.likes=quiet_chapel
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : My favourite chapel hour is when my cuffs needn't smell like anybody else's. | I can sit on a bare bench longer than I can rest on a soft doorstep.
b : What holds you there?
a : Knowing no load is going to come thumping down beside me till I choose to rise.

scene animals_1
when topic=animals self.dislikes=gulls
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A gull's rough on a slow eater. | I guard my oatcakes from overhead as well as from the wind.
b : Do you ever feed a gull?
a : It can have what falls once I've finished. I'd like the first say in the matter.

scene weather_1
when topic=weather
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : An autumn wind carries smoke away without needing any argument. | A breeze with leaves in it makes me stand a little taller.
b : Trying to catch the smell?
a : Trying to let this old smoky one blow right past the end of my tail.

scene home_1
when topic=home
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I air a cuff open or it'll bring yesterday indoors again. | I set smoky cloth apart from anything that's going near food.
b : Is the smell so strong?
a : It doesn't bother me half as much as biting an oatcake that tastes of yesterday's chimney.

scene smalltalk_1
when topic=smalltalk
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I turn my head away when somebody's face comes apart a little. | There's a look that asks for a minute without asking aloud.
b : Would you just walk off?
a : I'd put #nap# within reach first. Discretion needn't leave anybody barehanded.

scene prices_1
when topic=prices
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A square of decent linen pays for itself in small favours at every corner. | Cheap cloth may fray before the first wash gets all the soot out.
b : What would you buy first?
a : Good plain weave. Nobody wipes a nose more gently for a pattern of roses.

scene health_1
when topic=health
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : There's a strip of folded cloth between comfort and a purple shoulder. | I check for a ridge in a sling before it gets under my coat.
b : Would a thicker pad help?
a : A flatter pad, usually. More cloth can simply build the ridge a storey higher.

scene travel_1
when topic=travel here.region=ridgemere
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I like a landing wide enough to pass without touching elbows. | These city steps have taught me the worth of a level foot of stone.
b : Is that all you need to rest?
a : If somebody takes that load's trailing end, yes. Otherwise I'd like two feet.

scene times_1
when topic=times world.times=hard|lean
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : These narrow weeks I mend linen right out to the last good thread. | In a lean season even the corners of a napkin work for their keep.
b : What do worn corners become?
a : Little pads for a rubbing strap, if they've had their last turn near a face.

scene memories_1
when topic=memories
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I once saw an important face crumple in a place full of eyes. | Some memories deserve to stay folded up even in good company.
b : Would you say whose face it was?
a : No. The useful bit is remembering how much a moment of privacy cost me. Nothing.

scene day_1
when topic=day
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Smoke in my coat gets blamed for fires I've never gone near. | I sometimes get a worried sniff before I've so much as opened my mouth.
b : Does it trouble you?
a : I'd rather somebody checked than stood about wondering if the roof was alight.

scene friends_2
when topic=friends
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'd sooner quietly help a friend than announce I've arrived to save the day. | A kindness can be too big for the doorway it's meant to pass through.
b : How would you trim that kindness down?
a : Ask about one thing you can fix. Keep your clever explanation in your pocket.

scene gossip_1
when topic=gossip here.gossip=yes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : What went round was that #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. | Some talk has it that #topic.subject# #topic.claim#.
b : How much will you vouch for?
a : To having heard the words, yes. More than that costs another witness.

scene newcomer_1
when topic=newcomer
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I can point out a little patch of quiet to somebody new in town. | New feet on these stairs deserve a landing all to themselves sometimes.
b : Which mark means quiet?
a : Draw a clean square with a fingertip in the dust and say nobody minds a pause.

story smoke [topic=memories]
  : I put a napkin round a fresh oatcake to keep the smoke off it.
  : Then I remembered I'd been using the outside to wipe smoky fingers.
  b : Did the oatcake suffer?
  : Just one grey edge. I ate the edge and gave the clean middle away.

story bench [topic=faith]
  : I dropped a copper under a chapel bench and bent to look for it.
  : Down there I found a napkin so small it could only have belonged in a pup's pocket.
  b : What became of it?
  : I left it in clear sight on the seat and forgot my copper entirely till I got home.

story halves [topic=food]
  : I tried making two exactly equal pieces out of one buttered cake.
  : Each time I levelled the halves I had a little more crumb on the board.
  b : What was left to eat?
  : Two small bites and a lovely buttered heap. I haven't measured a gift so precisely since.

rule @linen
when concept=bark
does aside
cooldown 8h
say White corner in, smoky corner out. | A rolled cloth doesn't mind a short wait.

rule @dusk
when concept=bark here.time=dusk
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Good light for putting the heavy part down. | Save a little quiet for the last climb.

rule @faith
when concept=bark self.likes=quiet_chapel
does aside
cooldown 8h
say There's company in a quiet bench too. | Let somebody take a whole minute undisturbed.

rule @hand
when concept=bark self.likes=oatcakes
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Break the cake inside the cloth. Keep the crumbs. | Butter finds the cracks if you let it.
dlg resident.hub : You can speak to this side of me. The other side's keeping an eye on the bundle.
dlg resident.job [self.trade_words] : My day's called #self.trade_words#. The spare bit of cloth is my own idea.
dlg resident.news [world.news] : The words survived their journey like this. #world.news#.
dlg resident.gossip [here.gossip=yes] : A whisper says #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. I'll repeat the uncertainty with the words.
dlg resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : #topic.player#, have a piece of the quiet I've been saving.
dlg resident.bye : Keep a kind eye and a clean corner.

graft resident.hub
choice Is that cloth always clean inside? -> nap_roll
node nap_roll
say So long as I start with one clean square and roll it towards my wrist. Even a smoky sleeve can look after a thing properly.
choice Why carry it at all? -> nap_give
choice I'll leave it rolled up. -> hub
node nap_give
say There are little accidents folk wouldn't mind forgetting. Sometimes all the help that takes is giving a wolf a corner and looking past.
choice I'll leave it rolled up. -> hub
